Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 16:11:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 108/143] drm/sun4i: sun55i_de: hardware cursor plane (channel
 phys 7) + opaque LAY2/3

Testing the LAY1 overlay on the board (modetest plus register dumps)
showed that per-layer fetch works and LAY1 stacks above LAY0, but layers
inside one OVL channel stack opaquely by rectangle priority: a plain
AR24 0x77777777 buffer came out solid grey, with no per-pixel alpha
blending. Real transparency only exists in the Porter-Duff blend
between blender pipes ("four overlay windows to blend", "porter-duff
compatible blending" in the manual).

So:

- The LAY1..3 overlay planes only advertise opaque formats (XR24 and
  friends): advertising ARGB would invite the compositor to hand over
  translucent content that would show up opaque. All three are
  registered (zpos 1..3, immutable).

- The CURSOR plane is UI channel phys 7 (UCH1 of chn_cfg_mode=3) on
  blender pipe 1, with real alpha through SRCOVER and per-pipe premul.
  It also works while the primary scans out AFBC (the Plasma/Wayland
  case), where a cursor on a LAY would vanish because the AFBD turns off
  the OVL of the whole channel. Minimal phys 7 datapath as new RCQ
  blocks: OVL LAY0 + PARA + DS, VSU8 permanently bypassed (CTL=0 and
  glb_alpha=0xff staged at init: the alpha stage applies even in
  bypass), AFBD/CCSC at 0. No CDC or TFBD: mode 3 does not assign them to
  UCH1. de_top muxes: uch2core phys7 -> disp0 and port 2 (reset value
  0xa980, now explicit).

- Pipe enable/route/premul in the blender are now composed in
  sun55i_de_commit() (several planes share those registers), under the
  same arm_lock as the staging, so an arm can never apply a
  half-composed blender.

Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
